    "resolutionSummary": "The Aug 22 settlement-valley relief amplification introduced contour banding and a harsh grass-to-dirt sawtooth at ordinary player scale. Restored the valley base sampler to one gentle 51.2 m / 18-amplitude octave so authored settlement features own local elevation changes, and strengthened the exact capture-area regression to guard both neighbour continuity and total relief. Exact saved-camera real-player replay at the captured pose shows the large brown sawtooth transition gone and the foreground terrain calm and continuous. The capture note also called out the grass-to-dirt transition itself. A second fix feathers the road edge: KentridgeTownSurfaceCatalogue now emits a Dirt carriageway at the authored width plus five grassy shoulder bands per side, so the graded corridor blends back into the surrounding terrain instead of ending in a hard material step. KentridgeRoadShoulderRegressionTests asserts one carve strip, one carriageway core, and at least ten shoulder strips per road. This second fix was authored after the issue was first closed out and was recovered from an abandoned branch; it has not been replay-verified at the captured pose.",
